   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1337-opus, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** (head 7540a16)\n\n1. **High** (`App/SwiftHFRTests/Notifications/MPNotificationOpenTests.swift:107` and `:160`, not in the diff). `signedOutRecordsNothing` and `pageOneSeen` still compare `recorder.summaries == [NotificationSummary(unreadThreads: [10])]`. `recordReadState` now sends `unreadThreadMarks: [UnreadThreadMark(topic: 10, …)]`, and that field is part of the summary's synthesized equality. So both summaries now differ, and both App tests will fail on the macOS job. **Fix:** compare `.unreadThreads` or include the expected marks. Then grep `App/SwiftHFRTests` for other comparisons between `NotificationSummary` values.\n\n2. **High** (`NotificationLedgerThreadMarkTests.swift:101`). The line is 151 characters long. CI runs `swiftlint lint --strict`, so the Lint check fails (I ran it locally and got the `line_length` error). **Fix:** wrap the line.\n\n3. **Medium** (`NotificationLedger.swift:76-79`, LOT-091 \"went down … becomes the baseline\"). Record replaces each mark, even with a lower value. That lets a stale foreground list lower the baseline:\n   - At 10:00 the list loads: conversation 5 is unread with 1 reply.\n   - At 10:30 the background check sees 2 replies, sends a notification and records 2.\n   - Nothing reloads the list when the app comes back (`AppLifecycle.scenePhaseChanged`). The member opens conversation 7, `markOpened` calls `recordReadState`, and the stale page records 5 with 1 reply again.\n   - At 11:00 the check still sees 2 replies and notifies conversation 5 again.\n\n   **Fix:** keep the highest count and the latest date recorded for each conversation, as flags already do. A reply after a deletion still moves the date forward. Update the test and the spec to match.\n\n4. **Low** (`NotificationLedger.swift:47` vs `:77`). When one topic has two marks in a summary, diff reports news if any of them is ahead. Record keeps the last one, which can be lower, so every later check notifies the conversation again. **Fix:** reduce to the highest mark per topic in both diff and record, as `latestPerTopic` does for flags.\n\n5. **Low** (`NotificationLedger.swift:47`). The `where threads.contains(mark.topic)` filter in `diff` is not covered by any test. With the filter removed, all 31 tests still pass. The test `aMarkForAThreadThatIsNotUnreadIsIgnored…` never hits that case because it has no recorded mark for topic 8. **Fix:** add a test where conversation 8 is recorded, then read, and the summary still carries a mark for 8 that moved forward.\n\n6. **Detail** (`docs/lots/LOT-140-background-mp-check.md:47`, `:72`). Step 6 and the foreground paragraph still describe the summary with only the count and the unread set. They should also mention the marks.\n\n**Verified:** `swift test --filter NotificationLedger` at 7540a16: 31 pass; mutation of finding 5 stays green; `swiftlint --strict`: one error (finding 2); old JSON without the new key decodes and gets its baseline.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
