   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/i571-review-opus-r2, round 2): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 48a0a42\n\n1. **Medium**, `NotificationLedgerThreadMarkTests.swift` `aMarkForAConversationThatWasReadSinceIsIgnoredByDiff` (round-1 finding 5, still open). The test's second `record([5])` drops the mark of 8 before `diff` runs, so `before[8]` is nil and the result is empty either way. I removed `where threads.contains(topic)` from `NotificationLedger.swift:46` and all 33 tests still pass. The failure it should catch: the recorded set is {5,8}, 8 gets read, and a summary still carries a moved mark for 8, so 8 is notified while it is read. Fix: record `[5,8]` with marks, then call `diff` directly with `[5]` plus a moved mark for 8.\n2. **Medium**, `MessageListModel+Notifications.swift:22`. No test checks that the foreground record carries marks. `MPNotificationOpenTests` now compares only `.map(\\.unreadThreads)`, and `replyInAnUnreadConversation` calls `seenSummary` directly. Reverting `recordReadState` to the set-only summary breaks no test, yet a reply the member saw in the list would then be notified (an acceptance point of #571). Fix: in a `MessageListModel` test, assert that `recorder.summaries.last?.unreadThreadMarks` holds the row's `repliesCount` and date.\n3. **Low**, `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md:230`. GAP-191 still says \"A reply in an already-unread conversation waits on #571\", and the PR body has no `### Ledger` section. Fix: add a `gap-edit` block for GAP-191 (AGENTS §8).\n4. **Low**, `NotificationLedger.swift:83`. No test covers \"recording drops the marks of conversations no longer unread\" (LOT-091 spec): replacing the `.filter { threads.contains($0.topic) }` with `{ _ in true }` breaks no test. Fix: record `[5,8]`, then `[5]`, and assert that `unreadThreadMarks` lists only topic 5.\n5. **Detail**, the PR body is stale: it says 9 tests / 31 pass (now 11 / 33), and its `record` bullet leaves out the highest-wins rule.\n\nVerified: round-1 findings 1, 2, 3 (record), 4 fixed; 33 tests pass; `swiftlint --strict` clean; five mutations run (filter removed and no-drop survive).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
