   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/i571-review-opus-r3, round 3): APPROVE**, head 6518038\n\nAll round 2 findings are fixed. I checked each one with a mutation:\n- Removing `where threads.contains(topic)` in `diff` fails `aMarkForAConversationThatWasReadSinceIsIgnoredByDiff`.\n- Removing the drop filter in `record` (`kept.values.filter { threads.contains… }`) fails `recordingDropsTheMarksOfConversationsNoLongerUnread`.\n- Replacing the merge with `kept[topic] = mark` fails `aCountOrDateThatWentDownIsNotNewsAndDoesNotLowerTheBaseline`.\n- Reverting `MessageListModel.recordReadState` to the set-only summary makes `unreadThreadMarks` nil. `MPNotificationOpenTests/pageOneSeen` then expects `[UnreadThreadMark(topic: 10, …)]` and fails. I checked this by reading the code, since App tests do not run on Linux.\n- The GAP-191 `gap-edit` parses (`ledger.py check-body --pr 1337`: 1 block ok). It replaces only `SwiftHFR final`, drops the \"waits on #571\" sentence and matches the row's columns. No other doc still says #571 is pending.\n\nFindings:\n1. Detail: in the PR body, `### Tests` says \"11 tests\", but `NotificationLedgerThreadMarkTests` has 13. Fix the number.\n2. Detail: `MPNotificationOpenTests.swift:162` pins only zero values (`repliesCount: 0, lastPost: nil`). A mapping that drops the count or the date would still pass there. `MPBackgroundCheckTests/replyInAnUnreadConversation` covers it through the shared `seenSummary` (step 4 would notify), so this is not a gap.\n\nChecked: 34 tests pass; `swiftlint lint --strict` on the 9 changed Swift files clean; old-JSON decoding tested; idempotence; Swift 6 typing of the `seenSummary(of:)` overloads and the `\\.0` key path compiled with `swiftc -swift-version 6`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
